1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,243
Teacher midterm practice, question 9.

2
00:00:03,863 --> 00:00:07,443
In Figure 1, what does the slope of the curve at point A indicate?

3
00:00:09,143 --> 00:00:13,114
Point A sits on the straight elastic part of the curve, from O to B.

4
00:00:13,735 --> 00:00:18,991
There, sigma equals E times epsilon, so the slope is Young's modulus, E.

5
00:00:18,991 --> 00:00:21,475
A larger E means a stiffer material.

6
00:00:23,075 --> 00:00:25,011
The answer is D: stiffness.

7
00:00:25,831 --> 00:00:29,948
Strength is a stress value. Stiffness is a slope. Do not mix them up.
